        },
        {
          "sourceId": "src-861631518cfad575",
          "quote": "Our laboratory is studying central roles for novel membrane trafficking processes, under control of spatiotemporal lipid regulation, that coordinate dynamic cell structure. Using a foundation in genetic and cell biology experiments in the fruit fly, Drosophila, we are linking specific lipid kinase and phosphatase activities to cell remodeling.",
          "supports": [
            "research",
            "topics",
            "methods"
          ],
          "sourceUrl": "https://labs.biology.ucsd.edu/kiger/Amy_Kiger_Lab_at_UCSD/Home.html",
          "observedAt": "2026-10-16T03:18:14+00:00",
          "bodySha256": "9fd187dc3d2a44f676d2aac6f6d3a269cc5502584ec2ec274f97c4dab345afc0"
        },
        {
          "sourceId": "src-861631518cfad575",
          "quote": "Our research is currently focused in three major areas: (1) roles for phosphoinositide lipid regulation in cellular remodeling, (2) roles for autophagy in cellular remodeling, and (3) systems-biology approaches to understand cellular remodeling.",
          "supports": [
            "research",
            "topics",
            "methods"
          ],
          "sourceUrl": "https://labs.biology.ucsd.edu/kiger/Amy_Kiger_Lab_at_UCSD/Home.html",
          "observedAt": "2026-10-16T03:18:14+00:00",
          "bodySha256": "9fd187dc3d2a44f676d2aac6f6d3a269cc5502584ec2ec274f97c4dab345afc0"
        },
        {
          "sourceId": "src-861631518cfad575",
          "quote": "To address these problems, we are investigating questions specific to the dynamic organization of two distinct cell types, immune cells and muscle cells.",
          "supports": [
            "research",
            "topics"
          ],
          "sourceUrl": "https://labs.biology.ucsd.edu/kiger/Amy_Kiger_Lab_at_UCSD/Home.html",
